## 8. Competing Evolutionary Models

The thesis will compare four classes of evolutionary histories through formal statistical model comparison.

### Model A — Ancient multi-parental mosaic

$$
R. moschata + R. gallica + R. fedtschenkoana \rightarrow R. \times damascena
$$

with subsequent recombination.

### Model B — Hybridization plus subsequent introgression

$$
A + B \rightarrow H \rightarrow H + \text{introgression}
$$

Under this model, some ancestry blocks should show characteristics of more recent gene flow, including shorter block lengths and directional DFOIL signals.

### Model C — Incomplete lineage sorting

$$
\text{ancestral polymorphism} \rightarrow \text{lineage sorting} \rightarrow \text{discordant gene trees}
$$

No additional hybridization is required to explain discordance.

### Model D — Ghost introgression

$$
A + C \rightarrow A' \rightarrow A' + B \rightarrow R. \times damascena
$$

where C contributes ancestry through one of the primary parents rather than directly. This model addresses the possibility that *R. majalis* ancestry entered through *R. gallica* rather than through direct introgression into *R. × damascena*. **Critically, DFOIL is blind to ghost lineages**: a "proximal ghost" donor from within the sampled group can produce a false-positive signal of introgression from any lineage related to the ghost taxon.

