## Appendix G: Time-Aware HMM Extension

### G.1 Purpose

This appendix specifies the time-aware HMM extension for clonal propagation described in Section 12.2.

### G.2 Model specification

The transition probability becomes:

$$
P(z_i \mid z_{i-1}, c_i, t_{clonal})
$$

with two regimes:

| Regime | Condition | Transition probability |
|---|---|---|
| Sexual | \(t < T_{domestication}\) | \(P(z_i \mid z_{i-1}, c_i) \propto \exp(-r \cdot d_i \cdot t)\) |
| Clonal | \(t \geq T_{domestication}\) | \(P(z_i \mid z_{i-1}, c_i) \approx 1\) if \(z_i = z_{i-1}\) |

where \(d_i\) is the physical distance between windows \(i-1\) and \(i\), and \(r\) is the recombination rate.

### G.3 Parameter estimation

| Parameter | Prior | Range | Rationale |
|---|---|---|---|
| \(T_{domestication}\) | Log-uniform | 100–500 gen | Historical records |
| \(t_{effective}\) | Log-uniform | 10–1,000 gen | Per-block estimation |
| \(r\) | From LDhat/ReLERNN | Estimated | Not constant |
| \(f_{clonal}\) | Uniform | 0.9–1.0 | Clonal propagation |

### G.4 Implementation

```
Step 1: Define two-regime transition matrix
        ├─ Sexual regime: exp(-r * d * t)
        └─ Clonal regime: identity matrix

Step 2: Estimate T_domestication
        ├─ From historical records if available
        └─ From data if not (MCMC)

Step 3: Estimate t_effective per block
        ├─ Using topology weights from Twisst
        └─ Relative ages (not absolute)

Step 4: Run forward-backward algorithm
        └─ Modified for two-regime transition

Step 5: Report
        ├─ Posterior distribution of T_domestication
        └─ Relative ages per ancestry block
```

### G.5 Validation with methylation data

If bisulfite sequencing or methylation data are available:

```
Step 1: Extract CG/CHG methylation patterns
        └─ From bisulfite sequencing

Step 2: Reconstruct clonal propagation history
        └─ Following grapevine methodology

Step 3: Compare with HMM-inferred t_effective
        └─ Correlation > 0.7 expected

Step 4: If correlation is low
        └─ Flag as source of unquantified uncertainty
```

### G.6 Reporting

Results will be reported as:

1. **Posterior distribution** of \(T_{domestication}\)
2. **Relative ages** per ancestry block (with confidence intervals)
3. **Comparison** with methylation-based estimates (if available)
4. **Caveats** for absolute dating

